# Tarpaulin API Implementation Plan
 - comprehensive plan to implement the Tarpaulin API using Go, Google Cloud Platform, and Auth0.

## 1. Project Setup and Configuration
### 1.1 Google Cloud Platform Setup
- Create a new GCP project
- Enable required APIs:
  - App Engine API
  - Datastore API
  - Cloud Storage API
- Set up service account with appropriate permissions
- Configure local development environment with GCP credentials
### 1.2 Auth0 Setup
- Create an Auth0 account/tenant
- Set up a new API application
- Configure JWT settings (algorithms, token lifetime, etc.)
- Create the 9 required users with appropriate credentials:
  - admin1@osu.com
  - instructor1@osu.com , instructor2@osu.com
  - student1@osu.com through student6@osu.com
- Set up the same password for all users (as specified in the requirements)
- Configure callback URLs and CORS settings
