## 3. Implementation Steps
### 3.1 Authentication Setup
- Implement Auth0 integration for JWT authentication
- Create middleware to validate JWTs and extract user information
- Implement role-based authorization checks
### 3.2 Datastore Setup
- Create the users kind with required properties (id, sub, role)
- Design and implement the data model for courses and enrollments
- Implement advanced querying features (filtering, ordering, pagination)
### 3.3 Cloud Storage Setup
- Create a bucket for user avatars
- Implement file upload, retrieval, and deletion operations
### 3.4 API Endpoints Implementation User Endpoints
1. POST /users/login - Auth0 integration for user login
2. GET /users - List all users (admin only)
3. GET /users/:id - Get user details
4. POST /users/:id/avatar - Upload user avatar
5. GET /users/:id/avatar - Retrieve user avatar
6. DELETE /users/:id/avatar - Delete user avatar Course Endpoints
7. POST /courses - Create a course (admin only)
8. GET /courses - List all courses with pagination
9. GET /courses/:id - Get course details
10. PATCH /courses/:id - Update course (admin only)
11. DELETE /courses/:id - Delete course (admin only)
12. PATCH /courses/:id/students - Update course enrollment
13. GET /courses/:id/students - Get course enrollment
## 4. Testing
- Use the provided Postman collection for testing endpoints 1-9
- Create additional tests for endpoints 10-13
- Test authentication and authorization for all protected endpoints
- Test file operations for avatar endpoints
- Test pagination and filtering for courses endpoint
## 5. Deployment
- Configure app.yaml for App Engine deployment
- Deploy the application to Google App Engine
- Verify all endpoints work correctly in the deployed environment
- Update the Postman environment with the deployed URL
## 6. Data Population
- Pre-populate the Datastore with the 9 required users
- Set up the correct roles for each user
- Link Auth0 user IDs (sub) with Datastore user records
